{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 118, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-to-output edge with a conv adds a new path, whereas overwriting an existing op (especially a skip) removes a useful residual path."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, edge 3 is one of few routes to the output, so deleting it risks disconnecting or starving the output node."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input-to-node-2 edge, node 2 carries weaker (or zero) features, so a conv on node 2 -> 3 contributes less."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Activating node 1 with a conv creates new paths through edges 2 and 4, a bigger gain than replacing an existing op on edge 0."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with a parameter-free skip loses capacity, while replacing none or pooling with skip adds or improves a path."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for average pooling discards the most valuable op type, hurting more than replacing none, skip or 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0 is none, node 1 receives no input, so a conv on node 1 -> 3 processes zeros and has little effect."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 2 has no edge to the output, removing its input edge barely changes the network, so the usual loss from deleting a conv is smaller."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed is a large gain, whereas replacing an existing conv on edge 3 trades away capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With no direct input-to-output edge, the output relies on fewer paths, so a strong conv on node 1 -> 3 adds more relative value."}], "tok": 14494, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip